From 2d1c2b55e0feb971ad3a98e9616db6e28c2ad6a6 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Niklas Sheth <hi@niklassheth.com>
Date: Mon, 21 Sep 2026 15:47:13 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] HID: dockchannel: preserve baseline command and failure
 behavior

Drop global command cancellation, permanent timeout failure, and the additional command/TX synchronization. Restore baseline ACK handling, interface publication, and STM identification fallback. Pending commands retain the original timeout behavior.

Keep ring-registration serialization and cache its result so a failed registration is not reported as successful to a later interface. This is an untested bring-up trim, not a fix for pre-existing command races.
---
 drivers/hid/dockchannel-hid/dockchannel-hid.c | 287 ++++++++----------
 1 file changed, 121 insertions(+), 166 deletions(-)

